Tree Warden		 
	
		 
			

		 				
	 

	 	
 
	     


         The Tree Warden reports to the Town Administrator who reports to the Board of Selectmen. Responsibilities include: The care and maintenance of shade and ornamental trees within the town right-of-ways The removal of dead or hazard trees within the town right-of-way Emergency removal of storm damaged trees Dover Town Code Description of Responsibilities There shall be a Tree Warden appointed by the Board of Selectmen for a three-year term. The Tree Warden’s duties and authority shall include, but shall not be limited to, those specified in Massachusetts General Laws (MGL) Chapter 87, Section 2. View the full  Dover Town Code . Tree Emergencies For tree-related emergencies, please call the Police Department at 508-785-1130 Non-Emergency For non-emergency, questions, and concerns about the health or safety of a town tree, call (508) 785-0058 or email at  Kmccabe@doverma.gov 
     

 
